From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AtriOS <atrios@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] rtw88: add RTL8822E PHY/RF tables, efuse map and chip ops

Second stage of the Yandex Station Max Wi-Fi port, on top of
0010-rtw88-8822e.patch.  Stage (a) borrowed the whole 8822C PHY: the
board was expected to enumerate and load firmware, but association on
8822C analog/RF calibration was unlikely.

This adds the real 8822E tables converted from the GPL-2.0 vendor driver
github.com/Cohen0415/rtl8822cs-driver (halhwimg8822e_bb.c,
halhwimg8822e_rf.c, halrf_rfk_init_8822e.h):

 - rtw8822e_table.c: BB (2600 u32), AGC (7978), RF A (6334), RF B (6902),
   cal-init (5222), BB-PG (46 rows), txpower limits type0 (1488 rows) and
   type5 (868 rows).  The vendor arrays are kept verbatim, including their
   headline and 0x8/0x9/0xa/0xb/0x4 markers, and are run by
   rtw8822e_parse_tbl_phy_cond(), a 1:1 port of the vendor phy table
   engine; rtw88's cond matcher cannot express the vendor "greatest cut"
   fallback.
 - rtw8822c.[ch]: struct rtw8822e_efuse (vendor offsets from
   include/hal_pg.h; MAC at 0x16a), rtw8822e_read_efuse(),
   rtw8822e_ops (8822C ops with the 8822E efuse parser) and
   rtw8822e_rfe_defs covering the full rfe space.
 - point rtw8822e_hw_spec at the new tables, efuse parser and rfe defs.
 - Makefile: link rtw8822e_table.o into rtw88_8822c.ko.

The table generator lives outside the kernel tree in
mainline/tools/rtw88-8822e-tables.py.

Still 8822C: PHY/RF calibration code (IQK/DPK/TSSI/TXGAPK/spur), power
tracking delta tables, DPD, LDPC/STBC/etc. caps and WoW.  The logical
efuse size stays 768 (vendor EFUSE_MAX_MAP_LEN for 8822E is 2048 and the
HALMAC logical limit 416; 768 covers every field we read, but this is
unverified on hardware).

Signed-off-by: AtriOS <atrios@localhost>
---
